From ef5e3e1a1526ab9054d712ed649ced221ce76458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kloploid <10303425+kloploid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:47:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thor2: the status bar is an app's, always shown; SystemUI's
 panel never opens

With ro.config.thor2_statusbar (a service, NineSettings' StatusBarService):
- InsetsPolicy shows the status bar forcibly: no app can hide it, and every
  app's content stays below it.
- SystemServer binds the service right after starting SystemUI and keeps it
  bound (important, foreground), binding again after its app is updated.

With ro.config.thor2_shade, StatusBarManagerService always disables
SystemUI's panel and quick settings (DISABLE_EXPAND, DISABLE2_NOTIFICATION_SHADE,
DISABLE2_QUICK_SETTINGS): a swipe on the touchscreen no longer opens the stock
shade either. The shade is the app's screen (0010).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I07266286bbd353280d3d3a80582607074bf06e3f
---
